<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16565" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ex-ambĭo</span></b> , ii, ītum,
		4, v. n. and <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a.</i> (late Lat.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Neut.</i>, <i>to go round asking</i>,
				<i>soliciting</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ad Martyras,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cypr. Ep. 20</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>to ask</i>, <i>solicit</i> a person: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">viros, mulierculas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mamert. Grat. Act. ad Julian. 19</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">suffragium tui favoris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Symm. Ep. 7, 49</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exambita regia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 26, 7</span></i>
			.</div>
